/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
.DS_Store
node_modules/
# ...except vendored Node test fixtures: the corpus ships packages under a
# literal node_modules/ dir (warning_node_modules asserts DEP0005 is
# suppressed for callers inside one), and those files MUST be committed.
!conformance/vendor/node/test/fixtures/**/node_modules/
!conformance/vendor/node/test/fixtures/**/node_modules/**
/tests/wpt/checkout/
/bench/results/local/
/bench/sdk-fixtures/
.vscode/
.idea/
# Browser-driving (playwright-mcp / CDP-over-pipe) artifacts. The live MCP
# broker runs from the repo root, so its screenshots/snapshots land here.
/.playwright-mcp/
/oam-example-render.png
# `oam -e/-p` writes its throwaway script beside the cwd as
# `.oam-eval-<pid>.<ext>` and unlinks it on exit -- but a run that dies first
# leaves one behind, and two got committed into the vendored Node corpus that
# way (d691fda). Not scanned by the node-suite harness, so they sat there
# invisibly until a later cleanup deleted them and dirtied the release
# preflight. Ignored at any depth, since the cwd is wherever oam was invoked.
.oam-eval-*
